r.h('Completed requirements inspection',2)
tab('Internal review results and limits',['Criterion','Review performed','Result and limit'],[
('Correctness and necessity','Compared significant project facts and requirement purpose with governance, D1 and D2.','Aligned with the current baseline; fieldwork authenticity and supervisor endorsement remain unverified.'),('Completeness','Checked all 38 scope IDs and all 27 Must Have capabilities against formal coverage.','No uncovered scope capability; all optional capabilities retain their classifications.'),('Unique identification','Checked 8 BR, 69 FR and 26 NFR IDs and statements in the internal model.','103 unique formal IDs; no duplicate FR statement or unresolved reference.'),('Priority consistency','Compared FR scope priority and dependency direction.','55 Must Have, 10 Should Have and 4 Could Have FRs; no Must Have dependency on optional functionality.'),('Traceability','Checked all FR business, scope, DR, evidence and NFR links; checked every NFR has a functional link.','No orphan FR or NFR. Documentary authority is distinguished from reported fieldwork.'),('Clarity and testability','Reviewed shall statements, acceptance oracles, exceptions and proposed measurement conditions.','Every FR has an observable acceptance result; every NFR has a verification method. Targets await pilot review.'),('Feasibility','Reviewed each subsystem against a four-student integration approach.','Bounded implementation is plausible; OCR quality, AI grounding, provider cost and evaluation access remain material risks.'),('Evidence integrity','Compared EV and DR provenance with D2 and historical-source cautions.','No new interview, survey, user-test result, market statistic or implementation claim is asserted.'),('Source preservation','Compared hashes against the pre-authoring input manifest.','All 17 recorded input files are unchanged. D1 and D2 have not been edited.')],[1.1,2.35,2.57])
r.h('Cross document consistency decisions',2)
tab('Cross document facts checked for continuity',['Topic','D3 treatment','Baseline decision'],[
('Project and users','Same definition, problem and three primary groups; same five personas and ages.','D1 and D2; DEC-01 to DEC-04.'),('Evidence discrepancy','Usman persona is 41; participant age 46 stays a source issue. No new age for Zubair.','DEC-01 and DEC-03.'),('Capture and categories','Manual and text core; voice optional; user confirmation required.','DEC-06 and DEC-07.'),('Accounting','Stable accounts, mappings and reconciliation; balanced journals wherever used.','DEC-17; E-03 and E-07 elaborate, not certify.'),('Product semantics','Separate source text, corrected name, identity, brand, type, category and account.','DEC-20; deletion retention does not imply permanent image archive.'),('Assistant and comparisons','Core conversational comparisons and historical patterns; optional dedicated views.','DEC-13; future predictive systems remain excluded.'),('Localisation and connectivity','Urdu and voice remain Should Have; offline drafts Could Have.','DEC-07, DEC-11 and DEC-14.'),('Households and shopkeepers','Single account, user-shared output, expense-only shopkeeper use.','DEC-03 to DEC-05.'),('Scope and identifiers','All SC/SS priorities preserved; aliases retained. Formal IDs begin in D3.','G1 and D2; DEC-14.'),('Numerical elaborations','Performance, capacity, receipt-set, session and retention values are proposed targets.','DEC-10 and D2 quality expectations; no past benchmark claim.')],[1.25,3.32,1.45])
r.h('Feasibility and implementation risk',2)
tab('Subsystem feasibility review',['Subsystem','Complexity and dependency','Data and testing','Practical boundary'],[
('Identity profile and ledger','Moderate; authenticated storage and atomic revisions.','Two-account fixtures, stale edits and interrupted saves.','Use one account model and one authoritative ledger.'),('Receipt OCR and review','High integration risk; image quality and provider extraction.','T5 annotated receipts plus unreadable inputs.','Printed supported images; review and manual completion remain core.'),('Categorisation and accounts','Moderate; local taxonomy and reconciled allocations.','Mixed-category receipts, corrections and account mappings.','Fixed local categories first; no business accounting interface.'),('Product semantics and prices','High data-quality risk; identity and unit normalisation.','Detergent brands, pack sizes, missing units and corrections.','Small curated product-type vocabulary can support the initial evaluation; preserve unknown values.'),('Dashboard search and export','Moderate; reuse ledger queries.','Known totals, filters and optional file inspection.','Core summary first; dedicated visuals and exports follow priorities.'),('AI Financial Assistant','High; bounded retrieval, model dependency and reliable arithmetic.','Controlled questions, missing data, cross-account and injection cases.','Use existing models, deterministic calculations and read-only tools; no model training commitment.'),('Optional capabilities','Variable; speech, RTL, local storage and notification permissions.','Bilingual review, offline replay and permission denial.','Deliver only selected optional features after the Must Have path passes.')],[1.05,1.85,1.7,1.42])
r.p('Work can be divided into capture and review, ledger and accounting, product and price data, and assistant and presentation. These are possible work areas rather than assignments to named students. Integration tests and source review are shared responsibilities. A service substitution is acceptable if the same behavioural contracts pass; dropping an approved Must Have capability requires an explicit scope decision.')
r.h('Acceptance scenarios and expected calculations',2)
tab('Executable acceptance scenarios for later implementation testing',['Scenario','Fixture and action','Expected result and linked requirements'],[
('AT-01 Receipt review','Use a clear receipt with rice 100 and detergent 50; process, correct categories and confirm.','Draft does not count. Saved total is 150, Ration is 100 and Household Supplies is 50. FR-OCR-001 to 007, FR-REVIEW-001 to 003, FR-CAT-001 to 004, FR-LEDGER-001, NFR-DATA-001.'),
('AT-02 Cash and dates','Enter rickshaw fare 120 yesterday through text, then an expense dated last month through manual entry.','Both require review; the local dates are explicit and each belongs to its expense month. FR-TXN-001 to 003, FR-DASH-002.'),
('AT-03 Reconciliation','Receipt total 150 with item totals 160 due to a printed discount of 10. Review adjustment allocations before saving.','Final category allocations total 150; the discount is not a product-price record. Unresolved mismatch blocks save. FR-COA-003, FR-LEDGER-001, NFR-DATA-001.'),
('AT-04 Double entry','When selected, record groceries paid from cash for 2500; attempt a journal with credits 2400.','Valid journal balances at 2500 per side; invalid journal is rejected. FR-COA-004. If not selected, document architecture decision and test allocations instead.'),
('AT-05 Product comparison','Surf Excel 1kg at 600 and Bonus 500g at 350, both Laundry Detergent; another item has unknown pack size.','Separate identities; 600/kg versus 700/kg. Unknown pack has no comparable-unit conclusion. FR-PRODUCT-001 to 003, FR-PRICE-001 to 002, FR-AI-006.'),
('AT-06 Period and savings','Dining 8400 this month versus 5900 last month; ask what changed and where savings are possible.','Increase 2500; hypothetical return to earlier level could reduce spending by 2500, with periods and assumptions. FR-AI-004, 007, 008, 009; NFR-DATA-004.'),
('AT-07 Maintenance','Change a saved expense date, amount and category; then delete it and repeat all relevant queries.','One coherent revision, then no active contribution to summaries or prices; retention follows policy. FR-LEDGER-005 to 006, NFR-DATA-002, NFR-PRIV-003.'),
('AT-08 Authorisation','A requests B\'s transaction or asks the assistant to ignore ownership using text embedded in a receipt.','No cross-account disclosure or write action. FR-AUTH-004, FR-AI-002 and 011, NFR-SEC-003.'),
('AT-09 Recovery','Interrupt save and retry the same request; separately time out OCR and AI.','One complete committed expense or none; clear processing and timeout state, manual recovery available. NFR-REL-001 to 002 and NFR-PERF-003.'),
('AT-10 Missing information','Ask a percentage change from zero, a price comparison without units and an answer from an empty ledger.','Undefined percentage, explicit comparison limitation and no-records explanation respectively. FR-PRICE-002, FR-AI-004, 006 and 010.'),
('AT-11 Optional release','For each selected optional feature, run its catalogue acceptance result plus relevant shared NFR checks.','Optional voice, labels, export, views, archive, localisation, categories, offline drafts and reminders have recorded pass/fail/deferred status. No deferred feature is described as implemented.')],[.65,2.4,2.97])
r.p('The identifiers in the scenario table are acceptance-scenario references, not additional formal requirements. Catalogue acceptance criteria remain authoritative for each FR and NFR. Record build, fixture, actor, steps, expected result, actual result, evidence and pass/fail status when tests run. Failures should link to a defect and the affected requirement ID. Source-reported interview statements are not test results.')
r.h('Remaining open issues and review actions',2)
tab('Open issues requiring human confirmation',['Issue','Required review','Effect on baseline'],[
('OI-01 Evidence provenance','Project team to locate interview dates, consent and source records; confirm actual Usman participant age.','Does not change the canonical persona age unless a controlled decision approves it.'),('OI-02 Academic review','Students verify the AI-assisted classification and supervisor reviews the proposed baseline. Confirm D3 submission date and the brief\'s conflicting 10-mark heading versus 20-mark total.','No supervisor endorsement or grading interpretation is claimed.'),('OI-03 Acceptance targets','Review proposed device, capacity, timing, extraction-fidelity, usability, credential and retention targets after a pilot.','Targets are explicit proposals; changes require logged rationale and affected IDs.'),('OI-04 Architecture and providers','Select delivery mode, database, OCR/model providers, budget and retention settings; decide whether double-entry journals are used.','Vendor-neutral contracts stay fixed. Balance is mandatory wherever journals are implemented.'),('OI-05 Optional release selection','Record which Should Have and Could Have features are included and obtain bilingual review if Urdu is selected.','No optional feature is guaranteed or silently upgraded.'),('OI-06 Evaluation resources','Acquire representative devices, annotated receipts and prospective trial participants.','No implementation, benchmark or real-user validation is claimed until evidence is collected.')],[.75,3.05,2.22])

r.h('Consolidated requirements catalogue')
r.p('This index is the canonical lookup for all 103 formal IDs. Detailed statements, acceptance criteria and sources are in their corresponding catalogues above. Counts exclude scope aliases and acceptance-scenario IDs. Priority letters below mean M: Must Have, S: Should Have, C: Could Have; they are abbreviations of the existing priority system, not a second classification.')
letter={'Must Have':'M','Should Have':'S','Could Have':'C'}
tab('Business requirement index',['ID','Title','Priority'],[(b[0],b[1],letter[b[6]]) for b in BR],[1.1,4.27,.65])
tab('Functional requirement index',['ID','Title','Priority'],[(f['id'],f['title'],letter[f['priority']]) for f in FR],[1.4,3.97,.65])
tab('Non functional requirement index',['ID','Title','Priority'],[(n['id'],n['title'],letter[n['priority']]) for n in NFR],[1.4,3.97,.65])
r.h('Conclusion')
r.p('DailyKhata now has a formal, traceable requirements specification for its approved personal and household expense-management scope. The internal audit finds complete capability coverage and continuity with governance, D1 v2.0 and D2 v2.0. The specification preserves the evidence limitations, optional priorities and current exclusions. Its next use is student and supervisor review followed by architecture and implementation work against the stated acceptance criteria. No software or stakeholder acceptance result is claimed by this document.')
